Let $x, y, z$ be three distinct positive integers. The elementary symmetric polynomials in $x,y,z$ are $e_1 = x+y+z$, $e_2 = xy+yz+zx$, and $e_3 = xyz$. These integers satisfy the following system of equations:
\begin{align*}
 e_1 + e_2 + e_3 &= {A} \\
 e_1 e_2 &= {B} \\
 x^3+y^3+z^3 &= {D}
\end{align*}
